================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

No third-party CODE is vendored into this repository. Two third-party FONT FILES
are, as of 2026-07-30, under `bins/pl-gui/fonts/`; they are the first two entries
below. Five third-party LICENCE TEXTS are there too -- one covering those two
faces and one for each of the four that arrive through a crate -- because three
of those licences require their text to accompany every copy, and a path into a
Cargo registry is not something a recipient of `dist/` has.

Fonts embedded in the SHIPPED BINARY
------------------------------------

Six faces, 1,787,572 bytes, in polylinker.exe. Two are checked in here and four
arrive through a crate.

What the two vendored faces cost, measured rather than estimated: a release
build of `bins/pl-gui` went from 8,682,496 bytes at 0aa0f88 to 9,082,368 with
them in, +399,872 (+4.61%). The faces themselves are 373,552 of that; the
remaining 26,320 is what `lto = true` and `strip = true` did with the rest of
the change and is not attributable to the fonts alone. Font bytes reach `.rdata`
verbatim -- link-time optimisation does not compress them -- which is why they
are close to 1:1 on the executable and why the subsetting question below was
worth answering rather than assuming.

The two vendored ones came in with the 2026-07-30 typography pass. Everything
about them below was read from the bytes committed to this repository -- the
version from the file's own `name` table, the advance from its `hmtx`, the
licence from the `LICENSE.txt` in the same release archive -- and not from a
changelog, a README, or the repository badge on the upstream project. That
distinction is deliberate: `features/SOURCING.md` records the Sequence Ontology
entry being overturned because a machine-generated LICENSE restating a badge was
mistaken for independent corroboration, and a GitHub `spdx_id` is the same class
of artefact. api.github.com reports IBM/plex as OFL-1.1, and that is recorded
here as corroboration only.

TWO VERSION NUMBERS PER FACE, AND THEY DISAGREE ON PURPOSE. The npm package tag
and the typeface version are independent counters -- `@ibm/plex-mono@2.5.0` ships
a font whose `name` ID 5 reads "Version 2.005". Only the typeface version can be
read back out of the shipped .exe, so a record carrying only the tag cannot be
checked against the binary.

The sha256 of each committed file is the one a third party can verify against
IBM's own release archive, because neither face is subsetted or re-encoded. See
"Why neither Plex face is subsetted" below.

